prompt:
Build ONE self-contained HTML file: a 2D side-view cargo crane rendered on <canvas data-testid="simulation">. A rail at height 30 m spans x = -15..15 m. A trolley rides the rail; a cable of length L hangs from the trolley carrying a 1000 kg load (planar pendulum, g = 9.81, full nonlinear swing, pivot = trolley position). Trolley servo: max speed 5 m/s, max acceleration 2 m/s^2 toward its target. Hoist: cable length moves toward its target at 2 m/s. Load swing has linear angular damping 1.0 /s (crane sway-control). Integrate with a FIXED timestep dt <= 0.002 s (semi-implicit Euler or RK4). Draw the rail, tower, trolley, cable, load container, a target marker, plus a live readout of trolley x, cable length and sway angle.

MANDATORY benchmark API — a hidden automated grader calls exactly this; it must exist on window before load finishes, be deterministic for a given seed, and be independent of wall-clock time:
window.BENCH = {
  reset(seed) {},              // trolley at x = 0, cable length 20 m, load hanging straight down at rest, timeMs = 0
  step(ms) {},                 // advance physics by exactly ms milliseconds of simulated time using fixed-dt substeps
  perform(action, payload) {}, // 'move' with payload {x: number} sets the trolley target x (clamped to -15..15); 'hoist' with payload {len: number} sets the target cable length (clamped to 5..25 m)
  getState() { return {seed, timeMs, trolleyX, cableLen}; },
  getMetrics() { return {timeMs, trolleyX, loadX, loadY, swayDeg, cableLen}; }
};
swayDeg = load swing angle from vertical in degrees (0 = hanging straight down, sign indicates side). loadX/loadY = load position in meters in the same frame as the rail (rail y = 30). Include <button data-testid="reset">Reset</button> wired to BENCH.reset(1). The scene must also animate via requestAnimationFrame during free viewing. No external libraries — plain canvas 2D and vanilla JS only.
